**LOAN AGREEMENT**

January 14, 2021

**LOAN TERMS**

**1. Parties**

This Agreement is made by and between ABC Corporation, a Delaware corporation, with its principal place of business at 123 Main Street, Anytown, USA 12345 (hereinafter "ABC Corp"), XYZ Corporation, a Delaware corporation, with its principal place of business at 456 Oak Street, Anytown, USA 23456 (hereinafter "XYZ Corp"), and Defender Bank, a national banking association, with its principal place of business at 789 Elm Street, Anytown, USA 34567 (hereinafter "Defender Bank").

**2. Loan**

Defender Bank hereby agrees to lend to ABC Corp and XYZ Corp (hereinafter collectively, the "Borrowers") in the aggregate principal amount of one hundred million U.S. dollars ($100,000,000) (the "Principal Amount") for the purpose of financing the ongoing operations and capital expenditures of the Borrowers.

**3. Loan Documents**

This Agreement, together with the Loan Note executed by the Borrowers in favor of Defender Bank, the Security Agreement, and the other loan documents delivered by the Borrowers to Defender Bank (collectively, the "Loan Documents"), constitute the entire agreement between the parties with respect to the subject matter hereof.

**4. Interest**

The outstanding principal amount shall bear interest at the rate of 5% per annum, payable semi-annually in arrears on each June 30 and December 31 (the "Interest Payment Dates") commencing on June 30, 2021.

**5. Repayment**

The Borrowers shall repay the Principal Amount and accrued interest on the maturity date of the loan, which shall be December 31, 2025 (the "Maturity Date").

**INTEREST AND FEES**

**6.1 Late Charges**

If any amount payable hereunder is not paid when due, the Borrowers shall pay to Defender Bank a late charge equal to 5% per annum of the amount unpaid.

**7.1 Attorneys' Fees**

If any action or proceeding is brought to enforce any provision of this Agreement, the prevailing party shall be entitled to recover from the other party its reasonable attorneys' fees and costs incurred in such action or proceeding.

**DEFAULT AND REMEDIES**

**8.1 Default**

Any failure by the Borrowers to comply with any of their respective obligations under this Agreement or any of the other Loan Documents shall constitute an event of default.

**8.2 Remedies**

Upon the occurrence of an event of default, Defender Bank shall have the right, in its sole discretion, to demand immediate repayment of the Principal Amount, accrued and unpaid interest, and all fees and expenses incurred in connection with the collection of such amounts.

**8.3 Security**

The Borrowers hereby grant to Defender Bank a security interest in all of their respective assets as collateral for the loan.

